---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'What does local SEO actually help a Bend business do?',
    answer: 'The goal is to make your business easier to find when people nearby search for what you offer. That can include Google Search, Google Maps, your Google Business Profile, service pages, reviews, local content, and the website experience that turns visibility into calls, bookings, visits, estimates, or leads.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Do I need a separate page for every city or neighborhood I serve?',
    answer: 'Usually not. Location pages should reflect real services and real markets, not exist just to swap one city name for another. I would rather build fewer useful local pages than dozens of thin pages that do not help customers.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Can you help with Google Maps and my Google Business Profile?',
    answer: 'Yes. Local visibility often depends on the website and Google Business Profile working together, along with reviews, accurate business information, relevant service pages, local authority, and other supporting signals.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Is this only for small local businesses?',
    answer: 'No. I work across local businesses, multi-location programs, larger websites, technical SEO, content strategy, analytics, and AI search. The approach depends on the business problem and what you are trying to grow.'
  }
];

const serviceSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service',
  name: 'Bend Oregon SEO & Local Search Consulting',
  serviceType: 'SEO and Local SEO Consulting',
  description: 'SEO, Google Maps, local search, website strategy, content, and AI search visibility consulting for businesses in Bend and Central Oregon.',
  areaServed: {
    '@type': 'City',
    name: 'Bend',
    containedInPlace: { '@type': 'State', name: 'Oregon' }
  },
  provider: {
    '@type': 'Person',
    name: 'Mitchell Haw',
    url: 'https://mitchellhaw.com/'
  },
  url: 'https://mitchellhaw.com/services/seo-bend-oregon/'
};

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map((faq) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: faq.question,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: faq.answer }
  }))
};
---

<Layout
  title="Bend Oregon SEO Consultant | Local SEO & Google Maps"
  description="SEO, Google Maps, local search, website strategy, content, and AI search help for businesses in Bend, Oregon and Central Oregon."
  image="/images/bend-river.png"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(serviceSchema)} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />
  </Fragment>

  <main class="bend-page">
    <section class="bend-hero">
      <div class="container bend-hero-grid">
        <div class="bend-hero-copy">
          <p class="bend-kicker">LOCAL SEO · BEND, OREGON</p>
          <h1>Get your Bend business found by more of the right people.</h1>
          <p class="bend-hero-text">
            I help local businesses improve visibility in Google, Maps, and AI search, strengthen the pages customers land on, and turn more of that discovery into calls, bookings, visits, estimates, and leads.
          </p>

          <div class="bend-actions">
            <a class="bend-btn bend-btn-primary" href="/contact/">Talk About Your Business</a>
            <a class="bend-btn bend-btn-secondary" href="#bend-services">See What I Help With</a>
          </div>

          <div class="bend-proof-line">
            <span>Based in Bend</span>
            <span>Local + national SEO experience</span>
            <span>Google · Maps · AI Search</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bend-hero-media" aria-label="Bend and Central Oregon">
          <figure class="bend-main-image">
            <img src="/images/bend-river.png" alt="Deschutes River in Bend, Oregon" />
            <figcaption>Deschutes River · Bend</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <img src="/images/deschutes-brewery-bend-downtown.png" alt="Downtown Bend, Oregon" loading="lazy" />
          </figure>
          <figure>
            <img src="/images/black-butte-hike.png" alt="Central Oregon landscape near Black Butte" loading="lazy" />
          </figure>
          <div class="bend-media-note">
            <strong>Local search is local business.</strong>
            <span>The goal is not more traffic. It is more of the right customers finding you.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bend-owner-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="bend-heading split">
          <div>
            <p class="bend-kicker">WHAT BUSINESS OWNERS USUALLY ASK</p>
            <h2>“Why aren’t we showing up more?”</h2>
          </div>
          <p>
            That question can have a dozen answers. Your Google Business Profile may be weak. Your service pages may not match what customers search. Competitors may have stronger reviews, content, local authority, or websites. Sometimes the technical foundation is the problem. My job is to figure out which of those things actually matters for your business.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bend-outcome-grid">
          <article>
            <span>01</span>
            <h3>More visibility when someone needs what you do</h3>
            <p>Show up for the services, products, experiences, and local searches that can actually lead to business.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>02</span>
            <h3>A stronger path from Google to contacting you</h3>
            <p>Make service pages clearer, improve trust, and make the next step obvious once someone lands on your site.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>03</span>
            <h3>A shorter list of what is actually worth doing</h3>
            <p>Separate high-value work from the endless SEO checklist so your time and budget go toward the biggest opportunities first.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bend-services" id="bend-services">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="bend-heading split">
          <div>
            <p class="bend-kicker">BEND SEO SERVICES</p>
            <h2>What I can help you improve.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>
            You do not need to know which SEO term describes the problem before reaching out. Tell me what you want more of—calls, bookings, leads, traffic, map visibility, better rankings—and we can work backward from there.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bend-service-grid">
          <article class="bend-service-card featured">
            <div class="bend-service-label">LOCAL SEO + MAPS</div>
            <h3>Help nearby customers find you.</h3>
            <p>For businesses that depend on local calls, bookings, visits, appointments, estimates, or inquiries.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Google Business Profile review and optimization</li>
              <li>Google Maps and local-result visibility</li>
              <li>Reviews, listings, and business information</li>
              <li>Local competitor and opportunity research</li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article class="bend-service-card">
            <div class="bend-service-label">WEBSITE SEO</div>
            <h3>Make the website easier to find and understand.</h3>
            <p>For sites that are not ranking well, have confusing service pages, or need a stronger technical foundation.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Technical SEO and crawlability</li>
              <li>Site structure and internal linking</li>
              <li>Titles, headings, and page targeting</li>
              <li>Priority fixes instead of an endless audit</li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article class="bend-service-card">
            <div class="bend-service-label">SERVICE + LOCAL CONTENT</div>
            <h3>Build pages around what customers actually search.</h3>
            <p>For businesses that need stronger service pages, local landing pages, guides, FAQs, or content that supports real customer decisions.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Service-page strategy</li>
              <li>Local and service-area content</li>
              <li>Search-intent and topic research</li>
              <li>Useful content that supports conversion</li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article class="bend-service-card">
            <div class="bend-service-label">AI SEARCH + MEASUREMENT</div>
            <h3>Understand how newer search tools see your business.</h3>
            <p>For businesses wondering whether ChatGPT, Google AI, Gemini, Perplexity, and other discovery tools understand or recommend them.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>AI visibility and competitor benchmarks</li>
              <li>Source and citation research</li>
              <li>GA4 and Search Console measurement</li>
              <li>Recommendations connected back to SEO</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bend-market">
      <div class="container bend-market-grid">
        <div class="bend-market-media">
          <img class="market-large" src="/images/river-bend.png" alt="River scene in Bend, Oregon" loading="lazy" />
          <img src="/images/smith-rock-central-oregon.jpg" alt="Smith Rock in Central Oregon" loading="lazy" />
          <img src="/images/metolius-river.png" alt="Metolius River in Central Oregon" loading="lazy" />
        </div>

        <div class="bend-market-copy">
          <p class="bend-kicker">A BEND-SPECIFIC APPROACH</p>
          <h2>Different Bend businesses win search in different ways.</h2>
          <p class="lead">
            A roofer, dentist, realtor, brewery, guide service, clinic, restaurant, and vacation-focused business should not all have the same SEO strategy.
          </p>
          <p>
            A home-service company may care most about calls and Google Maps. A restaurant may need discovery around dining intent, reviews, menus, and visitors. A professional service may need strong service pages and qualified leads. A tourism business may need seasonal content and discovery before someone even arrives in Central Oregon.
          </p>
          <p>
            The strategy should reflect how your customers actually choose a business—not a generic local-SEO template.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bend-searches">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="bend-heading split">
          <div>
            <p class="bend-kicker">REAL SEARCH BEHAVIOR</p>
            <h2>Customers rarely search using your marketing language.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>
            They search for the problem, the service, the location, a recommendation, or a comparison. Good local SEO connects your business to those moments.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bend-query-grid">
          <div><span>Home services</span><strong>“roof repair Bend Oregon”</strong></div>
          <div><span>Healthcare</span><strong>“family dentist near me”</strong></div>
          <div><span>Real estate</span><strong>“Bend property management”</strong></div>
          <div><span>Food & drink</span><strong>“best lunch in Bend”</strong></div>
          <div><span>Visitor economy</span><strong>“things to do in Bend”</strong></div>
          <div><span>Professional services</span><strong>“accountant Bend Oregon”</strong></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bend-review">
      <div class="container bend-review-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="bend-kicker">WHAT I LOOK AT</p>
          <h2>A practical visibility review, not a mystery score.</h2>
          <p>
            I look at the parts of search that can actually affect your business, then turn the findings into priorities you can understand and act on.
          </p>
          <a class="bend-btn bend-btn-primary" href="/contact/">Ask About a Bend SEO Review</a>
        </div>

        <div class="bend-checklist">
          <div><span>Google Search</span><strong>What you rank for and what you are missing</strong></div>
          <div><span>Google Maps</span><strong>Local visibility and competitor position</strong></div>
          <div><span>Business Profile</span><strong>Accuracy, completeness, categories, reviews</strong></div>
          <div><span>Website</span><strong>Service clarity, structure, local relevance</strong></div>
          <div><span>Technical SEO</span><strong>Crawling, indexing, links, redirects, performance</strong></div>
          <div><span>Content</span><strong>Questions and search intent you are not covering</strong></div>
          <div><span>AI Search</span><strong>How newer discovery tools represent the business</strong></div>
          <div><span>Measurement</span><strong>Traffic, leads, visibility, and useful next steps</strong></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bend-area">
      <div class="container bend-area-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="bend-kicker">BEND + CENTRAL OREGON</p>
          <h2>Serve more than Bend? Build around your real market.</h2>
          <p>
            Some businesses serve one part of Bend. Others work across Central Oregon. Search strategy should match the areas where you genuinely do business—not create thin pages for every place name on a map.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bend-location-links">
          <a href="/services/seo-bend-oregon/"><span>Bend</span><b>Local SEO & visibility</b></a>
          <a href="/services/seo-redmond-oregon/"><span>Redmond</span><b>Local SEO & visibility</b></a>
          <a href="/services/seo-sisters-oregon/"><span>Sisters</span><b>Local SEO & visibility</b></a>
          <a href="/services/seo-sunriver-oregon/"><span>Sunriver</span><b>Local SEO & visibility</b></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bend-process">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="bend-heading split">
          <div>
            <p class="bend-kicker">HOW WE WOULD START</p>
            <h2>Start with the business goal, not an SEO checklist.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>
            Whether you need a focused project or ongoing support, the process should stay simple enough that everyone knows what we are trying to improve and why.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bend-process-grid">
          <article><span>01</span><h3>What do you want more of?</h3><p>Calls, bookings, estimates, appointments, website leads, local visibility, or stronger organic growth.</p></article>
          <article><span>02</span><h3>Where is the opportunity?</h3><p>Review the website, search results, Maps, competitors, content, technical setup, and local signals.</p></article>
          <article><span>03</span><h3>What should happen first?</h3><p>Prioritize the few changes most likely to matter and turn them into clear next steps.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bend-faq">
      <div class="container bend-faq-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="bend-kicker">COMMON QUESTIONS</p>
          <h2>Bend SEO FAQs</h2>
          <p>Plain-English answers to a few questions local owners commonly have before deciding what kind of search help they need.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bend-faq-list">
          {faqs.map((faq) => (
            <details>
              <summary>{faq.question}</summary>
              <p>{faq.answer}</p>
            </details>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bend-final">
      <div class="container bend-final-card">
        <div>
          <p class="bend-kicker">LOCAL SEO · BEND, OREGON</p>
          <h2>Want more of the right people finding your business?</h2>
          <p>Tell me what you do, where your customers come from, and what you want search to do better. We can start there.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="bend-btn bend-btn-primary" href="/contact/">Talk About Your Business</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .bend-page {
    --cream: #f6f4ee;
    --paper: #fffdf9;
    --ink: #1c2923;
    --copy: #59665f;
    --forest: #356b57;
    --forest-dark: #2b5847;
    --river: #2f6f8f;
    --sage: #e6eee8;
    --sky: #e9f2f5;
    --line: #d8ddd7;
    background: var(--cream);
    color: var(--ink);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .bend-page .container { width: min(1180px, 92%); margin: 0 auto; }
  .bend-kicker { margin: 0 0 15px; color: var(--forest); font-size: .7rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .bend-page h1, .bend-page h2, .bend-page h3 { color: var(--ink); }

  .bend-hero { padding: 72px 0 84px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #f7f5ef, #edf2ed); }
  .bend-hero-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0,.94fr) minmax(430px,1.06fr); gap: 68px; align-items: center; }
  .bend-hero-copy h1 { max-width: 720px; margin: 0 0 23px; font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 6.5vw, 6rem); line-height: .95; letter-spacing: -.06em; font-weight: 700; }
  .bend-hero-text { max-width: 670px; margin: 0 0 28px; color: var(--copy); font-size: 1.14rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .bend-actions { display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .bend-btn { display: inline-flex; min-height: 48px; align-items: center; justify-content: center; padding: 12px 19px; border-radius: 10px; font-size: .9rem; font-weight: 800; text-decoration: none; transition: .18s ease; }
  .bend-btn-primary { border: 1px solid var(--forest); background: var(--forest); color: #fff; }
  .bend-btn-primary:hover { background: var(--forest-dark); border-color: var(--forest-dark); transform: translateY(-1px); }
  .bend-btn-secondary { border: 1px solid #ccd5ce; background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink); }
  .bend-btn-secondary:hover { border-color: #aebbb2; transform: translateY(-1px); }
  .bend-proof-line { display: flex; gap: 12px 22px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 27px; color: #748078; font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 700; }
  .bend-proof-line span:not(:last-child)::after { content: '•'; margin-left: 22px; color: #aeb7b1; }

  .bend-hero-media { position: relative; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.35fr .75fr; grid-template-rows: 1fr 1fr; gap: 12px; min-height: 550px; padding-bottom: 50px; }
  .bend-hero-media figure { position: relative; margin: 0; overflow: hidden; border-radius: 18px; background: #d8dfdb; box-shadow: 0 18px 48px rgba(30,51,41,.08); }
  .bend-hero-media img { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; object-fit: cover; }
  .bend-main-image { grid-row: 1 / 3; }
  .bend-main-image figcaption { position: absolute; left: 15px; bottom: 15px; padding: 8px 11px; border-radius: 999px; background: rgba(255,255,255,.9); color: var(--forest); font-size: .7rem; font-weight: 800; }
  .bend-media-note { position: absolute; left: 28px; right: 28px; bottom: 0; display: flex; gap: 20px; justify-content: space-between; padding: 18px 20px; border: 1px solid #d4ddd6; border-radius: 14px; background: rgba(255,253,249,.96); box-shadow: 0 14px 32px rgba(28,41,35,.09); }
  .bend-media-note strong { color: var(--forest); }
  .bend-media-note span { max-width: 330px; color: var(--copy); font-size: .82rem; }

  .bend-owner-section, .bend-services, .bend-market, .bend-searches, .bend-review, .bend-area, .bend-process, .bend-faq, .bend-final { padding: 92px 0; }
  .bend-owner-section { background: var(--paper); border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .bend-heading.split { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr) minmax(320px,.75fr); gap: 72px; align-items: end; margin-bottom: 42px; }
  .bend-heading h2, .bend-market-copy h2, .bend-review h2, .bend-area h2, .bend-faq h2, .bend-final-card h2 { margin: 0; font-size: clamp(2.6rem,4.8vw,4.5rem); line-height: 1.02; letter-spacing: -.05em; font-weight: 700; }
  .bend-heading.split > p { max-width: 570px; margin: 0 0 3px; color: var(--copy); }

  .bend-outcome-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3,1fr); gap: 15px; }
  .bend-outcome-grid article { min-height: 260px; padding: 27px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 16px; background: #fff; }
  .bend-outcome-grid article > span { display: inline-grid; place-items: center; width: 34px; height: 34px; margin-bottom: 42px; border-radius: 9px; background: var(--sage); color: var(--forest); font-size: .71rem; font-weight: 800; }
  .bend-outcome-grid h3 { margin: 0 0 10px; font-size: 1.32rem; line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -.03em; }
  .bend-outcome-grid p { margin: 0; color: var(--copy); font-size: .93rem; }

  .bend-services { background: var(--cream); }
  .bend-service-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2,1fr); gap: 15px; }
  .bend-service-card { padding: 30px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 18px; background: #fff; }
  .bend-service-card.featured { background: var(--sage); border-color: #c8d9ce; }
  .bend-service-label { margin-bottom: 42px; color: var(--forest); font-size: .69rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .1em; }
  .bend-service-card h3 { margin: 0 0 10px; font-size: clamp(1.6rem,2.7vw,2.2rem); line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -.04em; }
  .bend-service-card > p { color: var(--copy); }
  .bend-service-card ul { margin: 22px 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .bend-service-card li { position: relative; padding: 8px 0 8px 22px; border-top: 1px solid rgba(89,102,95,.12); color: var(--copy); font-size: .9rem; }
  .bend-service-card li::before { content: '✓'; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--forest); font-weight: 800; }

  .bend-market { background: var(--sky); }
  .bend-market-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(430px,1.05fr) minmax(0,.95fr); gap: 72px; align-items: center; }
  .bend-market-media { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.25fr .75fr; grid-template-rows: 220px 220px; gap: 12px; }
  .bend-market-media img { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 16px; }
  .bend-market-media .market-large { grid-row: 1 / 3; }
  .bend-market-copy .lead { margin: 24px 0 12px; color: var(--ink); font-size: 1.13rem; font-weight: 650; }
  .bend-market-copy p:not(.bend-kicker):not(.lead) { color: var(--copy); }

  .bend-searches { background: var(--paper); }
  .bend-query-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3,1fr); gap: 12px; }
  .bend-query-grid div { padding: 22px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 14px; background: var(--cream); }
  .bend-query-grid span, .bend-query-grid strong { display: block; }
  .bend-query-grid span { margin-bottom: 22px; color: var(--forest); font-size: .68rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .bend-query-grid strong { font-size: 1.08rem; line-height: 1.25; }

  .bend-review { background: var(--sage); }
  .bend-review-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .9fr 1.1fr; gap: 72px; align-items: center; }
  .bend-review-grid > div:first-child > p:not(.bend-kicker) { max-width: 560px; color: var(--copy); }
  .bend-review-grid .bend-btn { margin-top: 12px; }
  .bend-checklist { overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid #c8d6cc; border-radius: 16px; background: rgba(255,255,255,.72); }
  .bend-checklist div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .72fr 1.28fr; gap: 18px; padding: 15px 18px; border-bottom: 1px solid #d2dcd4; }
  .bend-checklist div:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .bend-checklist span { color: var(--forest); font-weight: 800; }
  .bend-checklist strong { color: var(--copy); font-size: .86rem; font-weight: 600; }

  .bend-area { background: var(--cream); }
  .bend-area-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr .9fr; gap: 72px; align-items: center; }
  .bend-area-grid > div:first-child > p:not(.bend-kicker) { color: var(--copy); }
  .bend-location-links { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 10px; }
  .bend-location-links a { display: flex; min-height: 104px; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; padding: 17px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 13px; background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink); text-decoration: none; }
  .bend-location-links span { font-weight: 800; }
  .bend-location-links b { margin-top: 3px; color: var(--copy); font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 600; }

  .bend-process { background: var(--paper); }
  .bend-process-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3,1fr); gap: 14px; }
  .bend-process-grid article { padding: 27px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 15px; background: var(--cream); }
